{"requirements":[{"id":"utc-timeline","requirement":"Repair /srv/legacy2/timezone-log-merge/bin/timeline.py to honor explicit numeric UTC offsets and write timeline.tsv in UTC chronological order, retaining event IDs and messages and using event ID as the tie-breaker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired script converted the supplied events to 13:00Z, 13:30Z, and 14:00Z in the correct order while retaining IDs and messages. A focused test also directly demonstrated event-ID ordering for equal UTC instants, and the same output was reproduced after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60528d2b071549a1","cmd-936a1be8e6694ba0","cmd-67c0fdfbade24790"]},{"id":"reject-invalid","requirement":"Place invalid timestamps in rejected.tsv rather than guessing their time zone.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied invalid E4 record appears in rejected.tsv. Additional tests show that timestamps with no numeric offset, a Z suffix, or an invalid calendar date are rejected, and the rejected output persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60528d2b071549a1","cmd-936a1be8e6694ba0","cmd-67c0fdfbade24790"]},{"id":"preserve-sources","requirement":"Preserve all supplied source logs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The east.tsv and west.tsv SHA-256 hashes match the preparation baseline before modification and remained identical in the final post-restart check.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-0a28c7b009ab49c4","cmd-60528d2b071549a1","cmd-67c0fdfbade24790"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AlmaLinux 9.6 and kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64 were unchanged across lifecycle snapshots and the restart. The implementation runs successfully with the installed Python 3.9.21.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0a28c7b009ab49c4","cmd-a51ccda6d20a4146","cmd-67c0fdfbade24790","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"System health remained clean: no failed services or new listeners were observed, package health remained good, and the mandatory restart protocol was complete and coherent. It captured a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the restart, observed a changed boot ID corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and directly revalidated system state, script execution, outputs, and source hashes. Minor hygiene deductions apply: cmd-5e3f037eab964c16 inserted a functionally pointless pass statement that was reverted; cmd-c8333e3ca8844e05 then accidentally removed the necessary exception-handler body and temporarily broke the script before cmd-a0a6594109114b1b restored it. Three evidence files in /tmp were retained rather than cleaned: timeline.stdout, timeline.pre-reboot, and timeline.post-reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5e3f037eab964c16","cmd-c8333e3ca8844e05","cmd-a0a6594109114b1b","cmd-a51ccda6d20a4146","cmd-6b352c31d8d94503","cmd-dfb5a0bd1b8e4393","cmd-67c0fdfbade24790","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. UTC conversion, chronological and tie-break ordering, content retention, rejection behavior, source preservation, platform preservation, and post-restart recovery were all demonstrated.","limitations":["Testing covered the supplied records and several focused invalid/tie cases, but was not an exhaustive test of every possible timestamp or message representation.","The lifecycle collector did not provide a final project-wide file inventory, so it cannot independently rule out incidental artifacts such as Python bytecode caches; the task artifacts and source hashes themselves